INT. TELEGRAPH OFFICE, CANAL LOCK HOUSE - NIGHT

1868. Lamplight, wet floorboards, a brass key clicking on the long oak counter. Rain hammers the shutters. Water is coming under the door in a slow, steady sheet.

ELIAS VANTERPOOL, forties, stout, the clerk in charge, bends over the key. TOBIAS GRILL, twenties, his junior, stacks ledgers onto a high shelf. WINIFRED HALE, fifties, the lockkeeper's widow, stands by the stove with a shawl over her head. A girl, PRUDENCE, ten, sits on the counter with her boots held up out of the wet.

He taps out a line, stops, and taps it again. He does not look up.

ELIAS
(to the room)
Upstream station says the gates at Marlow are gone. Everyone move your things up.

TOBIAS
Gone how?

ELIAS
Gone like gone.

He grabs a ledger from the lower drawer and hands it up. He takes it, but it is heavy and he nearly drops it.

TOBIAS
(muttering)
Forty years of figures. Forty years, and we save the figures.

WINIFRED
Prue, up on the shelf with you. Now, please.

PRUDENCE
It's wet up there too.

She is lifted anyway. He sets her next to the ledgers and she hugs her knees.

ELIAS
Winifred, how long before it reaches the sill?

WINIFRED
An hour. Less if the Anderton sluice stays open.

He keeps tapping. She watches him tap, and neither of them says what both know about the sluice.

TOBIAS
(to Elias)
Sir, I could run to the lock house and shut it.

ELIAS
You could drown at the lock house.

TOBIAS
I could.

He pulls his coat on regardless. He is stopped at the door by a hand on his sleeve.

WINIFRED
Not you, boy. I know the wheel. I'll go.

ELIAS
Winifred --

WINIFRED
Elias, send your message.

She wraps the shawl tighter and opens the door. The rain comes in like a thrown bucket. She is gone.

Elias bends to the key. His hand is steady. His jaw is not.

TOBIAS
(to himself)
Should've been me.

PRUDENCE
(to everyone)
Is she coming back?

Elias taps. Tobias stares at the door. Nobody answers.
